# Working copies generated by Run-Deploy.ps1. It rewrites each script's :setvar
# block into _work\ and runs the copy from there, because sqlcmd gives an in-file
# :setvar the same precedence as -v and the later assignment wins. Those copies
# therefore contain environment-specific values (server, database names) and are
# regenerated on every run.
_work/

# Deploy and test logs. They contain server names, database names, row counts and
# full result sets from the target instance, so they are deliberately not
# published. Keep them with the change record instead.
_logs/

# Ad-hoc parameterised copies of the product's own scripts (e.g. 053, which needs
# a runtime password filled in). NEVER commit these - they hold credentials.
#
# ANCHORED, not a bare *.RUN.sql. Git on Windows matches ignore patterns
# case-insensitively, so the bare form also matched
#   kAM2/01-database/source-objects/kArchiveManagerAdmin/Tables/arch.Run.sql
# which is one of the 63 ":r" includes of the core deploy bundle. It sat on disk,
# stayed out of the repository, and a clone therefore could not deploy the product
# at all - the one failure a self-contained package must not have. Found
# 2026-09-17 by listing the IGNORED files rather than trusting the rule.
#
# The parameterised copies only ever land at the repository root or in _work/,
# so anchoring costs nothing and cannot reach into kAM2/.
/*.RUN.sql
/*.RUN2.sql
/*_runtime.RUN.sql
_work/*.RUN.sql

# Local editor / OS noise
.vs/
*.suo
*.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
